 ("h2", "Music and Dance"),
 ("ul", ["Nāṭyaśhāstra shaped dance, drama and music; storytelling traditions include Rajasthani puppetry and **paṭṭachitra** (Odisha, West Bengal, Andhra Pradesh).", "Two streams: **Hindustani** (north) and **Carnatic** (south, largely unaffected by Persian influence).", "**Dhrupad** flourished under Raja Mansingh Tomar of Gwalior (late 15th c.); **Tansen** joined **Akbar's** court as one of the nine ratnas.", "Modern **sitar** and **tabla** evolved in these centuries from older instruments such as the pakhāwaj."]),
