 ("ul", ["After invasions, **purdah** and **ghūnghaṭ** became more common, mainly in north India; public life of women declined.", "**Razia Sultan** (13th c.), first and only woman ruler of the Delhi Sultanate; led armies, opened schools; opposed by nobles.", "**Nur Jahan** (early 17th c.): issued orders, coins in her name, patron of art and trade.", "In the **south**, elite women stayed in administration; temple donations; **Tirumalamba** wrote *Varadambika Parinaya*."]),
